{
  "chapter": "durable-execution/temporal-in-forty-minutes",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "Six nouns, and the split everything depends on: if it could return a different answer on",
    "a second call, it is an activity.",
    "Workflow code is orchestration the engine may replay freely. Activity code touches the",
    "world and is never replayed \u2014 only its recorded result is reused.",
    "That is the difference from graph checkpointing. A checkpointer resumes the graph and",
    "re-executes the node; here a completed activity never runs again.",
    "The mistake to expect is a database read in workflow code, because reads feel harmless.",
    "The row can change between the original run and the replay, so reads are activities.",
    "Retries are first class: attempts are bounded and the backoff is a deterministic",
    "exponential, so both tracks compute the same schedule.",
    "The event history is the durable, ordered log of one execution, and replaying against it",
    "is what rebuilds the workflow's in-memory state."
  ],
